ine-5","page_id":"/docs/command-line","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/command-line#commands","content":"Commands"},"1259":{"id":"/docs/command-line-6","page_id":"/docs/command-line","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/command-line#three-rules","content":"Three rules"},"1260":{"id":"/docs/command-line-7","page_id":"/docs/command-line","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/command-line#output-and-exit-codes","content":"Output and exit codes"},"1261":{"id":"/docs/command-line-8","page_id":"/docs/command-line","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/command-line#shape-the-output","content":"Shape the output"},"1262":{"id":"/docs/command-line-9","page_id":"/docs/command-line","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/command-line#versions","content":"Versions"},"1263":{"id":"/docs/command-line-10","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line","content":"Read, search, create and update STLabs tickets from your terminal or a script. Every command comes from the published API contract."},"1264":{"id":"/docs/command-line-11","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#access","content":"Access to the STLabs API is not open yet. This release cannot sign in or call the API. To request access, email support@stlabs.com. A refused sign-in or call prints two lines and exits with code 10."},"1265":{"id":"/docs/command-line-12","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#get-started","content":"`login` signs you in and `org set` picks the organization every call acts on. `status` shows the host, whether you are\nsigned in, and which organization is set. `logout` removes the stored token. See the two\nsections below for each."},"1266":{"id":"/docs/command-line-13","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#sign-in","content":"`login` stores the token in the OS keychain. On Linux that is the Secret Service when one is\navailable; on a headless machine set `STLABS_TOKEN` instead. It reads the token from stdin and\nrefuses one given as an argument, which would end up in your shell history:"},"1267":{"id":"/docs/command-line-14","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#sign-in","content":"`STLABS_TOKEN` in the environment takes precedence over the keychain; use it in CI and scripts.\nWith neither, a command stops with `stlabs: not signed in` and sends nothing."},"1268":{"id":"/docs/command-line-15","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#sign-in","content":"On macOS the keychain ties an entry to the program that wrote it. After reinstalling `stlabs`, the\nnext command can show a system dialog and wait with no output. Click Always Allow, or set\n`STLABS_TOKEN`."},"1269":{"id":"/docs/command-line-16","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#sign-in","content":"While access is closed, nothing is written to the keychain and nothing is sent."},"1270":{"id":"/docs/command-line-17","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#organization","content":"Every call names the organization it acts on:"},"1271":{"id":"/docs/command-line-18","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#organization","content":"The slug is not a secret, so it is stored in its own file (`~/.config/stlabs/config.json` by\ndefault), not the keychain. `STLABS_ORGANIZATION` in the environment takes precedence; use it in\nCI and scripts. With neither set, a command stops with `stlabs: no organization set` and sends\nnothing."},"1272":{"id":"/docs/command-line-19","page_id":"/docs/command-line","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/command-line#commands","content":"| command                          |                            |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `stlabs people availability get` | Get someo