ors"],[153,"Errors"],[252,"Errors"],[324,"Errors"],[352,"Errors"],[405,"Errors"],[432,"Errors"],[547,"Errors"],[577,"Errors"],[615,"Errors"],[641,"Errors"],[672,"Errors"],[711,"Errors"],[742,"Errors"],[800,"Errors"],[847,"Errors"],[881,"Errors"],[933,"Errors"],[955,"Errors"],[980,"Errors"],[1023,"Errors"],[1051,"Errors"],[1074,"Errors"],[1107,"Errors"],[1131,"Errors"],[1196,"Errors"],[1354,"Every build is made from one API version and sends it on every call. A build keeps working on\nits API version until that version is retired. New commands come with a new build."],[1270,"Every call names the organization it acts on:"],[1253,"Every command, the body syntax, output options, exit codes and idempotency."],[1338,"Example output of tickets get"],[738,"File a ticket"],[20,"File a ticket `/tickets`"],[743,"File a ticket for somebody. The requester must resolve to a person in this organization, or the request is refused. The response carries `routing`: `settled` once the ticket has a queue and a state, `pending` until then, while automatic routing may still change the queue, state or priority."],[347,"Find queues"],[21,"Find queues `/queues:search`"],[353,"Find queues by name or by who works them. Each one comes with its settings and the caller's own role in it. Results are in name order, paged with a cursor. Live counts are `null`, never zero, on any queue whose tickets this caller cannot all read. For operators."],[1070,"Find similar tickets"],[22,"Find tickets like this one `/tickets/{ticket}/similar`"],[40,"GET /people/{person}/availability"],[249,"GET /queues/{queue}"],[321,"GET /queues/{queue}/operators"],[931,"GET /reference/priorities"],[952,"GET /reference/queues"],[1049,"GET /reference/relationship-types"],[1105,"GET /reference/states"],[844,"GET /tickets"],[797,"GET /tickets/{ticket}"],[638,"GET /tickets/{ticket}/comments"],[1020,"GET /tickets/{ticket}/relationships"],[1071,"GET /tickets/{ticket}/similar"],[248,"Get a queue"],[796,"Get a ticket"],[39,"Get avail